<item><title>Rubber Softfall Renewal - Emerald Botanical Gardens and Rotary Park Blackwater</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Council requires the supply and installation of certified impact-attenuating rubber softfall surfacing in the form of a modular individual tile system at existing playgrounds including approximately 300m2 at the Emerald Regional Botanic Gardens and approximately 400m2 at Rotary Park, Blackwater. <br /><br />The installed softfall system must be certified to comply with the relevant Australian Standards for impact attenuation and playground safety, including the required Critical Fall Height for the playground equipment. The finished motif is to be a like for like pattern using the existing colour palette. The surface is to be uniform, free from trip hazards and constructed to the required levels and drainage requirements.<br /><br />The contractor is to provide all labour, plant, equipment, materials, testing, certification and associated works necessary to deliver a fully compliant and completed installation. Temporary construction fencing to fully isolate the project area from public access is to be supplie...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Central Highlands Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 28/Sep/2026 12:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP523808<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Sport, Recreation Equip, Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=5f1c1ad2c46e4450a4039fb8a1af076cs523808sbfe2d966aa884191b5a30f84da5d0f3fs1604</link>
