<pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 19:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Sport, Recreation Equip, Services</category>
</item>
<item><title>Central Queensland Hospital and Health Service (CQHHS) Condition Assessment Audit 2026-2029</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The State of Queensland through Queensland Health (the Client), invites you to submit an offer for the provision of suitably qualified and experienced consultant to undertake comprehensive condition assessments of Queensland Health assets for the Central Queensland Hospital and Health Service CQHHS Condition Assessment Audit 2026-2029 Project in accordance with the Invitation documents.<br /><br />The purpose of this Scope of Works is to engage suitably qualified and experienced consultants to undertake comprehensive condition assessments of Queensland Health assets. The assessments will provide accurate, consistent and auditable information on asset condition, remaining useful life, defects, risks and renewal requirements. This information will support strategic asset management, maintenance planning, capital investment planning and long-term infrastructure renewal across Queensland Health.<br /><br />For detailed information on the specific goods / services sought under this Request for Offer, please review...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Health Infrastructure Queensland<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 17/Sep/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP524007<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Dean Schipplock Email: dean.schipplock@health.qld.gov.au Tel: 0422321231<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Architecture, Design, Planning, Construction & Operation, Engineer, Research, Tech services, Real Estate & Property Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 8]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/PublicTenderAccess.aspx?id=1dc719c79b354cc2821db76d30995a21s524007</link>
