<item><title>MidCoast Council Concrete Processing Tender Waste Services</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> MidCoast Council is seeking an experienced contractor to crush, grind, screen and process stockpiled concrete, bricks and tiles under a five-year, non-exclusive, as-required contract.<br /><br />Processing will be undertaken at Council’s Waste Management Centres at Taree, Gloucester and Stroud. The Contractor will produce the following finished products:<br /><br />20 mm minus road base;<br /><br />40 mm minus road base; and<br /><br />80 mm minus cobbles.<br /><br />The Contractor must provide all personnel, supervision, mobile processing plant, loaders, screening and magnetic-separation equipment, water-based dust suppression, traffic controls, site establishment, product testing, stockpiling, cleaning, reporting and demobilisation required to complete each processing occurrence.<br /><br />For standard Service Requests, the Contractor must commence site establishment within 21 calendar days. For urgent Service Requests, commencement is required within seven calendar days, with up to four urgent requests pe...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> MidCoast Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 30/Sep/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP523183<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Mining & Quarrying & Oil & Gas, Waste Management & Landfill<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 5]]></description>
