<item><title>Upgrade to Planet Creek Stock Route Facilities</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Planet Creek Stock Route Reserve is an important infrastructure asset that provides a designated area for the movements, agistment and watering of travelling livestock within the region. The reserve supports Council’s Rural Lands unit by maintaining access to essential stock route networks and provides facilities that assist livestock producers, transport operators and authorised users travelling through the area.<br /><br />The existing facilities at Planet Creek have reached an age where upgrades and renewal works are required to ensure the reserve remains functional and compliant with current operational and animal welfare standards. These upgrades have been approved in consultation with the Stock Route Management Network, with Queensland Government grant funding secured to support the delivery of the works.<br /><br />The Plant Creek reserve is the most heavily agisted reserve within the Central Highlands Region. This primary reserve is located along the Blackwater-Rolleston Road.<br /><br />The succe...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Central Highlands Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 14/Sep/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP523765<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation, Farming & Animal Services & Equip<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
