<item><title>Lithgow Mountain Bike Trails Construction Expressions of Interest (EOI Phase)</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Central Tablelands Mountain Bike Club (CTMBC) invites suitably experienced and capable specialist mountain bike trail construction contractors to register their interest in the design and construction of the Lithgow Mountain Bike Park trail network at State Mine Gully, Lithgow NSW.<br /><br />This Expression of Interest (EOI) is Stage 1 of a two-stage procurement. It is a capability and capacity assessment only. No price is sought at this stage. Respondents assessed as capable will be shortlisted and invited to submit a tender under a subsequent selective Request for Tender (RFT).<br /><br />This EOI has been prepared in accordance with the CTMBC Procurement Procedure and is an open and transparent process consistent with best practice. It is conducted via VendorPanel and administered by PMO 360 Pty Ltd on behalf of CTMBC.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Central Tablelands Mountain Bike Club<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 15/Sep/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP522952<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Paul Smith Email: paulsmithmonger@gmail.com Tel: 047543518<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation, Horticulture & Arboriculture<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
