<item><title>RFQ260197 - Emerald Saleyards Dip Yards Redesign Construct</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Central Highlands Regional Council (Council) operates the Emerald Saleyards and has a clearing dip which services thousands of cattle each year. Council's current objective is to upgrade existing areas and utilise spaces that will overall improve operational use and provide a safer and more reliable working environment. <br /><br />Council have provided draft/concept drawings for the addition of gates to the Emerald Saleyards dip area, currently it has 90-degree passages with pull down portable panels. Construction to the area will optimize cattle flow and accessibility, improving livestock welfare, driving higher processing volumes and increased sales.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Central Highlands Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 14/Sep/2026 04:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP522954<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation, Railway, Tramway and Track<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
