<item><title>2026.069 - Development of a Laratinga Trails and Boardwalks Masterplan</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Laratinga Wetland is a highly popular and well used community and environmental asset with over 8,000 people accessing the wetland via its trails each week. To ensure access to the wetland is safe, equitable and maximises community and environmental outcomes, a review of the trails and boardwalk infrastructure is proposed. To help with this task, the Mount Barker District Council (“Council”) is seeking to engage a suitably qualified consultant to review existing Laratinga wetland trails and boardwalk layout and infrastructure, associated access issues and opportunities and to develop a master plan to inform future development upgrades and renewals.<br /><br />The existing Laratinga trail network and boardwalks was constructed when the wetlands were first developed in the late 1990’s. The boardwalks are now at end of life, with one section having been closed to public access for over 2 years. The boardwalks consist of 1 main section that crosses basin 3 and includes a viewing platform and 2 smaller sections in...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Mount Barker District Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 14/Sep/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+09:30) Adelaide time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP522544<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Architecture, Design, Planning<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
