<item><title>BHTSP Contract Administration Panel - Aug 26</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Department of Transport and Main Roads (TMR) is seeking applications for new applicants to join the BHTSP Contract Administration Panel.<br /><br />This application process is only for new applicants wishing to join the BHTSP Contract Administration Panel (existing BHTSP Contract Administration Panel Members are not permitted to apply for this process).<br /><br />The Department of Transport and Main Roads (TMR) is delivering the Bruce Highway Targeted Safety Program (BHTSP). The Bruce Highway is a vital 1,673 kilometre north-south corridor in Queensland, connecting Brisbane to Cairns. In January 2025, the Australian and Queensland governments announced a joint funding commitment of $9 billion towards the BHTSP to enhance safety and uplift deficient sections of the highway to achieve a three-star rating.<br /><br />The BHTSP focuses on sections of the Bruce Highway between Gympie and Cairns with a high safety risk.<br /><br />Projects to be delivered through the BHTSP will be awarded to prequalified contr...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Department of Transport and Main Roads<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 08/Sep/2026 11:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP522472<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 4]]></description>
