<item><title>TRC000584 Southern Cross Oval Light Upgrade</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Southern Cross Reserve Oval is a Council-managed, multi-use sporting facility comprising a single irrigated oval with a turf wicket block and supporting amenities. The oval is classified as a Class 1 sports field within Toowoomba Regional Council’s sports field hierarchy due to the quality of the playing surface, the level of supporting amenities and the availability of oval lighting.<br /><br />The facility supports a high level of seasonal community sport. During summer, it is used for Toowoomba A Grade Cricket competition, including limited-over, night fixtures and T20 night games. During winter, the oval supports Downs Rugby competition and AFL Darling Downs competition. Key user groups operating from Southern Cross Reserve Oval include Toowoomba Cricket Incorporated, Bears Rugby Union and South Toowoomba Bombers AFL.<br /><br />The current oval lighting configuration includes three 30 metre TP EK30M GM poles, and three 25 metre TP EK25M GM poles, fitted with a combination of Philips MVP507 luminaires and...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Toowoomba Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 15/Sep/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP522459<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, ELEC, Lighting, Equip & Services, Sport, Recreation Equip, Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 16]]></description>
