<item><title>Pick of the Crop 2027-28 expansion to Far North Queensland</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> HWQld is Queensland’s dedicated prevention agency established to prevent chronic disease and improve health equity, with a focus on healthy eating, physical activity and obesity.<br /><br />HWQld has committed to implementing a whole-school healthy eating program in all state primary schools across Queensland to increase children’s vegetable and fruit consumption. Pick of the Crop (POTC) is a whole school, multi-strategic, evidence-based healthy eating initiative developed by HWQld; it is flexible and designed by schools to focus on their unique community needs and school environment. <br /><br />HWQld seeks to engage one or more Implementation partner/s in a two-year agreement to support delivery of POTC across Far North Queensland's Department of Education (DoE) regions.<br /><br />Implementation Partner/s will be responsible for recruiting and managing a regional coordinator and supporting school engagement, implementation and stakeholder collaboration.<br /><br />Key activities are expected to include:<br...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Health and Wellbeing Queensland<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 18/Sep/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP521762<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Community & Social Services, Food & Beverage Products, Healthcare Services, Training & Development<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 5]]></description>
