<category>Horticulture &amp; Arboriculture</category>
</item>
<item><title>WT25-25/26 Pechey PAC Dosing and WTP Upgrades</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Toowoomba Regional Council (TRC) is seeking quotations for the supply and installation of a new Powdered Activated Carbon (PAC) dosing system. This PAC system is to be installed at the Pechey Water Treatment Plant located on Grapetree Road. The scope of works involved are detailed in this document and consists of a mixture of mechanical, electrical, and control systems integration.<br /><br />The existing PAC dosing system and layout has resulted in issues such as improper powder feed, blockages, inaccurate dosing, and corrosion of the hopper frame. Due to these issues and the age of the unit, Council is looking at replacing this PAC dosing system.<br /><br />To cater for the new PAC dosing system, several Control System upgrades are required to be undertaken. This includes a PLC Platform upgrade and the installation of a new RIO network. Several other plant modifications are also required including waste pit level instrument control, automated UV duty selection and ATV600 upgrade.<br /><br />Pechey Water Tre...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Toowoomba Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 09/Oct/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP522175<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 13]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=843ed3b01f3e4bffaa602695507098f0s522175s786e232eacbb4e31b23c50bf234a0226s1611</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">843ed3b01f3e4bffaa602695507098f0</guid>
<pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 19:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Water &amp; Sewage</category>
</item>
<item><title>T27011 - Statutory Planning Public Notice Installation Services Panel</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Contract No. T27011 - Statutory Planning Public Notice Installation Services Panel<br /><br />Tenders are invited for the Statutory Planning Public Notice Installation Service.<br /><br />Council is seeking submissions from suitably qualified and experienced contractors for the provision of public notification signage services associated with statutory planning applications. The services include the production, installation, maintenance, inspection and removal of public notice signs at locations throughout the municipality, in accordance with Council requirements and relevant legislative obligations.<br /><br />The successful contractor will be required to provide a reliable, responsive and customer-focused service that supports Council’s statutory planning processes. Tenderers will be expected to demonstrate their experience in delivering similar services, their capacity to meet service timeframes, quality assurance processes, reporting capabilities, and commitment to workplace health and safety. Council int...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> City of Stonnington<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 14/Sep/2026 12:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP522128<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Printing & Distribution Services, Signs & Barriers<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 1]]></description>
