<item><title>RFT CT2027006 Livestock Marketing Centre: Sheep Loading Ramp Renewal D&amp;C</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Wagga Wagga City Council (Council) are improving the loading ramps of the Livestock Marketing Centre (LMC) sheep delivery yards. The ramps, located in the northeast corner of the site, were constructed with the original facility and have reached the end of their useful life. This increases the risk of slips, injuries and creates potential workplace safety and animal welfare concerns.<br /><br />The project aims to replace the original ramps with modern equipment to ensure safe operating conditions for animals, staff, and operators. Pavement renewal at the base of the ramps will also be undertaken.<br /><br />The desired outcome of this RFT is to enter into a Lump Sum Contract with an appropriately experienced Contractor for the Design & Construction of new ramps and pavement renewal in accordance with the tender documentation.<br /><br />The Scope of Works under this RFT is to design new loading ramps, remove the existing ramps, remediating the pavement, and installing new loading ramps.<br /><br />The works ...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Wagga Wagga City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 15/Sep/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP522219<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Products & Materials, Construction & Operation, Farming & Animal Services & Equip<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 9]]></description>
