<item><title>RFT260087 Construction of Blackwater Recycled Water Pipeline Stage 2 Valve Station</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Background Information<br /><br />Central Highlands Regional Council is seeking a suitably qualified and experienced contractor to undertake the construction of the Blackwater Recycle Water Pipeline Stage 2 Valve Station at Hunter Street, Blackwater.<br /><br />The works form part of Council’s recycled water infrastructure and involve the fabrication, supply and installation of new valve station pipework and associated equipment and protective structural cover, together with connections to existing pipeline infrastructure. The works include integration with the existing DN300 HDPE Stage 3 pipeline and DN200 HDPE rising main, installation of Principal-supplied and Contractor-supplied equipment, and associated civil, excavation, backfilling, testing, commissioning and reinstatement works.<br /><br />The existing DN100 effluent pipeline is required to remain operational during construction until the new work is complete, and the final connections can be undertaken.<br /><br />The successful Contractor will be re...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Central Highlands Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 18/Sep/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP521924<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Products & Materials, Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation, Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 12]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/PublicTenderAccess.aspx?id=435fe571f6864f5b99682dcff2957017s521924</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">435fe571f6864f5b99682dcff2957017</guid>
<pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Building Products &amp; Materials</category>
<category>Building Trade, Repairs, Maint.</category>
<category>Construction &amp; Operation</category>
<category>Water &amp; Sewage</category>
</item>
