</item>
<item><title>RFT260086 - Long-Term Residual Waste Solution — Standardised Site Assessment</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Central Highlands Regional Council (CHRC) invites suitably qualified consultants to submit tenders for RFT260086 – Long-Term Residual Waste Solution – Standardised Site Assessment.<br /><br />The engagement is for a strategic waste planning consultancy to undertake a comprehensive, evidence-based assessment of Council's long-term (30–50 year) residual waste disposal solution. The successful consultant will reconcile the remaining life of the existing Lochlees Resource Recovery and Landfill Facility, model long-term residual waste demand, develop a standardised assessment methodology, evaluate potential long-term disposal options against the Queensland Landfill Siting, Design, Operation and Rehabilitation Guideline (ESR/2015/1627), and prepare a defensible options report to inform future Council decision-making.<br /><br />This is a desktop strategic planning and technical assessment. It does not include detailed engineering design, statutory approvals, land acquisition, or intrusive field investigations, whic...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Central Highlands Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 17/Sep/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP519432<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Engineer, Research, Tech services, Indust. Production, Manufacturing, Management Advisory Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
