<item><title>Tender for land within the Lansdown Eco-Industrial Precinct</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Lansdown Eco-Industrial Precinct (LEIP or Precinct) is positioned as a major industrial precinct for environmentally responsible advanced manufacturing, technology and processing activities. The Precinct is located approximately 40 kilometres south of the Townsville central business district in the suburb of Calcium and comprises approximately 2,200 hectares extending east from the Mingela State Forest and Lansdown Creek towards the Flinders Highway. Townsville City Council (Council) acquired the land in 2001 after its previous use by the Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organisation as a pasture research site.<br /><br />LEIP is supported by strategic access to the Port of Townsville, major road and rail corridors, the North Queensland Gas Pipeline, the Woodstock Ergon Substation and planned industrial water infrastructure. Since 2019, Council has undertaken several open market processes for land within the Precinct. Those processes resulted in conditional land allocations across advanced ...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Townsville City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 31/Oct/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP520903<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Architecture, Design, Planning, Fuel & Oils, Indust. Production, Manufacturing, Power Generation, Trans & Distrib., Railway, Tramway and Track, Utilities<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 2]]></description>
