<item><title>Penrith City Library Smart Device Application</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The contractor is required to deliver a comprehensive mobile library application (iOS and Android) with the following key capabilities:<br /><br />• Core Features:<br /><br />User account access, catalogue search across physical and digital collections, real-time item availability and location and item renewals synced with the Library Management System (LMS).<br /><br />• Integration:<br /><br />Seamless integration with LMS and RFID systems, with LMS-agnostic functionality. The app must connect to a wide range of existing digital platforms (e.g., Libby, BorrowBox, Freegal, Beamafilm, StoryBox, Humanitix) and support future integrations.<br /><br />• Digital Access:<br /><br />Ability to download and access eBooks and eAudiobooks directly within the app.<br /><br />• User Experience:<br /><br />Intuitive, user-friendly design that meets accessibility standards (e.g., WCAG), and allows in-library borrowing via mobile devices.<br /><br />• Administration:<br /><br />A staff-facing CMS for content management, pl...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Penrith City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 11/Sep/2026 06:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP521402<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : IT & Telecomms<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 7]]></description>
