<item><title>Connecting Kin (T210) and Equipping Kin (T211), – South East Region (Region wide service)</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Customer (being the Department of Families, Seniors, Disability Services, and Child Safety, (the department)) is seeking quotes for one service provider to deliver the following two service types:<br /><br />Connecting Kin (T210) services are responsible for targeted family mapping and engagement leading to new family connection or family members making application to be assessed as kinship carers (engagement focused). Outsourced non-government Connecting Kin services may work in conjunction with current regional Child Safety Finding Kin teams.<br /><br />Equipping Kin (T211) services are responsible for supporting initial kinship carer assessments, including provisional approval assessments. Services will provide all necessary supports to have kinship carers approved so they can commence caring (assessment focused). Outsourced non-government Equipping Kin services may work in conjunction with current regional Child Safety Finding Kin teams.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Families, Seniors, Disability Serv & Child Safety<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 14/Sep/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP521511<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Community & Social Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 4]]></description>
