<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Package is being delivered through a partnership-based approach, working across Queensland Government, with up to six government partner agencies, to implement strategic funding partnerships. The Commission has established a group with representatives from each partner agency, to support coordination, collective impact measurement, shared learning and governance oversight across the package. <br /><br />The partnerships fund a range of initiatives including, a mix of place-based activities, community and local council grant programs, cross-sector collaboration, and activities that strengthen workforce capability, service integration, and policy and practice across systems. Activities are delivered across metropolitan, regional, and remote Queensland. Timing of initiatives will be staggered across financial years FY2025/2026 to mid FY2028/2029.<br /><br />The Commission requires an external Supplier to undertake an independent evaluation of the previous Grants and the Package, including development of an e...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Queensland Mental Health Commission<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 11/Sep/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP521201<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Jasmine Repia Email: jasmine.repia@qmhc.qld.gov.au Tel: 3244 9254<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Management Advisory Services, Training & Development<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
