<item><title>Provision of a Signage Design Manual</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The City of Clarence is seeking an experienced environmental graphic designer or signage design specialist to develop a practical and contemporary Signage Design Manual that provides a consistent, accessible and durable approach to signage across Council-managed places and facilities. The Manual should provide clear design and technical guidance so Council can design, procure, install, maintain and progressively replace standard signage across Clarence.<br /><br />It is desirable that the consultant has demonstrated experience in city-wide or local government signage systems, including design strategy, documentation and implementation guidance.<br /><br />The purpose of this project is to develop and implement a comprehensive Signage Design Manual for the City of Clarence. The manual will ensure that future public signage across the city is consistent, clear, and effective, aligning with urban design best practice, accessibility standards, and the visual identity of City of Clarence.<br /><br />This manual wi...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> City of Clarence<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 09/Sep/2026 03:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Hobart time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP520759<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Rebecca-Ann Riseley Email: rriseley@ccc.tas.gov.au Tel: 6217 9767<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Graphical, Photographic & Art, Marketing & Communications, Printing & Distribution Services, Signs & Barriers<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
