<item><title>Mobile Crushing Services</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Council is seeking a suitable contractor to deliver mobile crushing and screening services to various gravel pits within the Central Darling Shire Council area.<br /><br />The term of the contract is 2 years with an option to extend for a further 12 months if deemed appropriate. MW21 contract framework is applied with expected value to remain below $2 million over a 2 year period.<br /><br />The successful contractor will be required to supply all plant, equipment, labour, supervision, fuel, maintenance and associated resources necessary to undertake the crushing, screening and stockpiling of gravel and road-making materials. The materials produced will be used for the maintenance, rehabilitation and construction of Council's road network and other infrastructure works.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Central Darling Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 04/Sep/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP520318<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Reece Wilson Email: wilsonr@centraldarling.nsw.gov.au Tel: +61 08 8083 8800<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Mining & Quarrying & Oil & Gas<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 5]]></description>
