<pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 23:23:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Community &amp; Social Services</category>
<category>Engineer, Research, Tech services</category>
<category>Healthcare Services</category>
<category>Training &amp; Development</category>
</item>
<item><title>Floor Finishes Upgrade at MSAC and Lakeside Stadium</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> MSAC conducts annual slip-resistance testing across the facility. Testing undertaken in in February 2024, August and November 2025, and March 2026 confirmed that 47 areas across MSAC and LAKE failed to meet minimum slip-rating standards. <br /><br />Slip-resistance tests have revealed that sections of the existing flooring — comprising sheet vinyl, stair nosings, coated concrete, and ceramic tiles — do not meet the required safety classifications. As a result, the State Sports Centres Trust (SSCT) intends to treat or replace non-compliant flooring in affected areas, so they meet slip-rating standards.<br /><br />The scope includes:<br /><br /> 1)	Treatment to areas specifically listed in the attached specification document.<br /><br /> 2)	Removal and disposal of existing floor coverings. <br /><br /> 3)	Removal and disposal of existing stair nosings.<br /><br /> 4)	Supply and installation of new floor coverings.<br /><br /> a)	 All materials must achieve or exceed their respective minimum required classificat...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> State Sport Centres Trust<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 07/Sep/2026 11:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP519565<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Products & Materials, Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Office Related Supplies & Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 16]]></description>
